          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Wagner's Middle Period</strong><br>\nDuring the middle period of his career, Wagner completed some of his most significant operas, including \"Tristan und Isolde,\" which introduced new ideas about harmony and dissonance in music.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Exile and Influence</strong><br>\nWagner's revolutionary political activities in the 1840s led to his exile from Germany. This period of his life was significant as it influenced his later works, which often reflected his ideals about society and art.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Ring Cycle</strong><br>\nWagner's monumental work, \"Der Ring des Nibelungen,\" a cycle of four operas, took him over 25 years to complete. It is one of the pinnacles of the operatic repertoire and reflects his maturity as a composer.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
